title: Agricultural Policy
new-page: true
is-card: true
on-arrival: agricultural_policy_timer += 6; month_actions += 1
view-if: spd_in_government = 1 and (agriculture_minister_party = "SPD") and agricultural_policy_timer == 0
card-image: img/portraits/BaadeFritz.jpg
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet

= Agricultural Policy

Farming has never been the SPD's strongest field, but the countryside matters. Small and medium farms are closing every year, investors are buying up farmland in the East, and the farmers who blocked the motorways with their tractors in 2024 have not forgotten. City voters, meanwhile, want cheaper and better food.

- @land_reform
- @agricultural_finance
- @pro_consumer
- @state_buyer
- @root: Do not enact any policies for now.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@land_reform
title: Farmland for Farmers
subtitle: -1 budget. Stop investors and holding companies from buying up farmland.
unavailable-subtitle: Requires 1 budget.
choose-if: budget > 0
on-arrival: budget -= 1; land_reform += 1; coalition_dissent += 1; rural_spd += 5*(1-dissent); rural_afd -= 4*(1-dissent); fdp_relation -= 5; cdu_relation -= 2; left_strength += 5; left_dissent -= 5; rural_policy += 1; agriculture_goal_completed += 1
max-visits: 4

A new law gives local farmers the first right to buy land, closes the loophole that let investors buy farms through share deals, and lets the Länder cap land prices. The FDP calls it an attack on property; many farmers in Brandenburg and Saxony-Anhalt call it overdue.

@agricultural_finance
title: Support for Family Farms
subtitle: -1 budget. Credit, insurance and investment aid for small and medium farms.
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; agricultural_finance += 1; rural_spd += 5*(1-dissent); rural_afd -= 3*(1-dissent); peoples_party_support += 1; center_dissent += 5; left_dissent += 4; rural_policy += 1; economic_growth += 0.2;

We fund cheap credit, crop insurance against drought and investment aid for new barns. Some on the left of our party ask why we are subsidising landowners.

@pro_consumer
title: Cheaper Food
subtitle: -1 budget. Cut VAT on basic food.
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; pro_consumer += 1; workers_spd += 4*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 4*(1-dissent); pensioners_spd += 2*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1 if recession_seen; inflation -= 0.2; economic_growth += 0.1;

We cut VAT on bread, vegetables, milk and other basic foods. Shoppers notice it at the till. [? if recession_seen and (in_weimar_coalition or in_grand_coalition) : Our coalition partners call it an expensive giveaway. ?]

@state_buyer
title: Fair Prices
subtitle: -2 budget. Ban selling food below the cost of production and limit the power of the supermarket chains.
choose-if: budget >= 2
on-arrival: budget -= 2; state_buyer = 1; rural_spd += 5*(1-dissent); rural_afd -= 3*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 2*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1 if (in_grand_coalition or in_weimar_coalition); fdp_relation -= 5; cdu_relation -= 2; peoples_party_support += 1; rural_policy += 2; capital_strike_progress += 1; inflation += 0.1; economic_growth += 0.2;
max-visits: 1

Following the example of Spain, the four big supermarket chains can no longer force prices below what it costs to produce the food. A public agency monitors contracts and fines abusers. Farmers are pleased, and the retail lobby is furious.
